{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01SeGG3BrnR5mewGs6vHfVfW", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Li-Fi\"}, {\"url\": \"https://cacmb4.acm.org/news/114974-using-light-to-send-data-across-the-room\"}, {\"url\": \"https://siliconangle.com/?p=215155\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.slideshare.net/slideshow/seminarpp-59478423/59478423\"}, {\"url\": \"https://vitmumbai.vitmumbai.hosting.acm.org/story.php?id=14\"}, {\"url\": \"https://vitmumbai.acm.org/story.php?id=14\"}, {\"url\": \"https://etcentric.org/tag/photophone\"}, {\"url\": \"https://physicsworld.com/a/how-big-ideas-can-change-the-world-the-revolutionary-potential-of-lifi/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://lifi.co/harald-haas/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://lifi.co/?p=35\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:03:44.764Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Li-Fi TEDGlobal 2011 Edinburgh University professor visible light communication", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01EzPvQcbHwZ5N1KvpnYHkG3", "content": [{"title": "Li-Fi", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Li-Fi"}, {"title": "114974 using light to send data across the room", "url": "https://cacmb4.acm.org/news/114974-using-light-to-send-data-across-the-room"}, {"title": "UPDATED 08:15 EDT / JANUARY 20 2015", "url": "https://siliconangle.com/?p=215155"}, {"title": "www.slideshare.net", "url": "https://www.slideshare.net/slideshow/seminarpp-59478423/59478423"}, {"title": "vitmumbai.vitmumbai.hosting.acm.org", "url": "https://vitmumbai.vitmumbai.hosting.acm.org/story.php?id=14"}, {"title": "vitmumbai.acm.org", "url": "https://vitmumbai.acm.org/story.php?id=14"}, {"title": "LED Technology as Option for Wireless Data Transmission", "url": "https://etcentric.org/tag/photophone"}, {"title": "how big ideas can change the world the revolutionary potential of lifi", "url": "https://physicsworld.com/a/how-big-ideas-can-change-the-world-the-revolutionary-potential-of-lifi/"}, {"title": "Harald Haas", "url": "https://lifi.co/harald-haas/"}, {"title": "Harald Haas", "url": "https://lifi.co/?p=35"}]}, "Harald Haas, a mobile communications professor at the University of Edinburgh, introduced the term \"Li-Fi\" in his 2011 TEDGlobal talk. The results agree on the core facts:\n\n- **The term and the talk:** Wikipedia credits Haas with coining \"Li-Fi\" at TEDGlobal in Edinburgh in 2011 (1-2). His talk was titled \"Wireless Data from Every Light Bulb\" (9-11).\n- **The demonstration:** Haas used an LED lamp to send a video of blooming flowers, which was projected behind him (2-3). The demo took place on 12 July 2011 (4-4).\n- **Background:** Visible light communication (VLC) is the broader umbrella term, and Li-Fi is one application of it (1-7). Edinburgh's VLC research began in 2008 and led to the spin-out pureLiFi in 2012 (3-3, 3-4).\n\nSources differ on some details. One says Haas began his research in 2004 (4-4), while another says VLC research at Edinburgh began in 2008 (3-4). Reported demo speeds also vary: about 10 Mbit/s in one 2011 report (7-3). Later work reached much higher rates, including lab speeds of 224 Gbps at Oxford (8-12)."], "durationSeconds": 6.3956698339999996, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01SeGG3BrnR5mewGs6vHfVfW", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
